<section xml:id="review">
  <title>Review</title>

      <ul>
        <li><p>What does it mean for a set of vectors to be <em>linearly independent</em>?</p></li>
        <li><p>What does it mean for a set of vectors to <em>span</em> a vector space?</p></li>
      </ul>

      <exercise xml:id="ex-independent-extension">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Let <m>\vec{v}_1,\dots,\vec{v}_k\in V</m>, and suppose they are linearly independent.
            Let <m>\vec{u}\in V</m>. Then
            <m>\vec{v}_1,\dots,\vec{v}_k,\vec{u}</m> are linearly independent if and only if
            <m>\vec{u}\notin\operatorname{span}(\vec{v}_1,\dots,\vec{v}_k)</m>.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </exercise>
    </section>